dsh-fa-rtl README · How it works：Every chat row DSH ships is laid out left-to-right (LTR); Persian text inside it is bidi-reordered by the Unicode algorithm, but the *base direction* stays LTR — so Persian paragraphs stay left-aligned and punctuation drifts to the wrong edge.

The web-standard fix is `dir="auto"`. Since plugins cannot touch the React-rendered DOM, this plugin uses its exact CSS equivalent:

```css
unicode-bidi: plaintext;
text-align: start;
```
